      "multiplicity": "none",
      "no_survivor": "not applicable -- a floor always exists. If the floor exceeds the planning minimum on an endpoint, every bar reading that endpoint rises accordingly and that is the finding.",
      "adopts": "nothing",
      "also_published": "the +/-10% A-steps arms, as RECIPE SENSITIVITY beside the floor, never as the floor: a step change is a treatment, not a null",
      "frame_disclosure": "measured in the incumbent teacher frame and the M7 data mix, A leg only with the B checkpoint fixed. An arm differing in its B leg has a larger floor and no bar may read such an arm until that floor is measured too.",
